{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>Moses and Aaron and his sons.</b> And camped next to them was the standard of the camp of Judah, and those encamped around it — Issachar and Zebulun. Good for the righteous, good for his neighbor — for the neighbors of Moses, who was occupied with Torah, became great in Torah, as it is said: ״יְהוּדָה מְחֹקְקִי״ (Psalms 60:9); ״וּמִבְּנֵי יִשָּׂשכָר יוֹדְעֵי בִינָה וגו׳ מָאתַיִם״ (I Chronicles 12) — heads of sanhedrin; ״וּמִזְּבוּלֻן מֹשְׁכִים בְּשֵׁבֶט סֹפֵר״ (Judges 5:14) (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:18.516120945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}